  "question": {
    "choices": [
      "A. The cholesterol levels in the supplement group were lower after treatment compared to before treatment.",
      "B. Both groups had cholesterol levels above 200 mg/dL before treatment.",
      "C. The placebo group showed a decrease in cholesterol levels after treatment, while the supplement group did not.",
      "D. The cholesterol levels of the supplement group decreased significantly after treatment compared to the placebo group."
    ],
    "correct_answer": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanation": "Choice D is the best answer because it correctly describes the data shown in the graph, which indicates that the cholesterol levels of the supplement group decreased significantly after treatment, supporting the hypothesis that the dietary supplement is effective in lowering cholesterol levels compared to the placebo group. The graph shows that the supplement group started with a cholesterol level of 210 mg/dL and dropped to 190 mg/dL after treatment, while the placebo group started at 215 mg/dL and increased to 230 mg/dL. This distinct change in levels between groups provides evidence supporting the hypothesis.\n\nChoice A is incorrect because it does not compare the supplement group to the placebo group, failing to address the key aspect of the hypothesis. Choice B is misleading, as it only states that both groups had cholesterol levels above 200 mg/dL before treatment without indicating any changes or comparisons after treatment. Choice C is wrong because the data shows that the placebo group actually had an increase in cholesterol levels after treatment, which contradicts the statement.",
    "paragraph": "<p>In a recent study, researchers at the University of Health Sciences investigated the effect of a new dietary supplement on the cholesterol levels of adults. The study involved two groups of participants: one group received the supplement, while the other group was given a placebo. The researchers measured the cholesterol levels of both groups after eight weeks of treatment to determine if the supplement had an impact on lowering cholesterol. The hypothesis was that adults taking the dietary supplement would exhibit lower cholesterol levels compared to those taking the placebo.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"image\">\n<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"568.280625pt\" height=\"425.259189pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 568.280625 425.259189\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-02-22T07:58:53.960919</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.10.8, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 425.259189 \nL 568.280625 425.259189 \nL 568.280625 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: #ffffff\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 50.980625 339.21382 \nL 561.080625 339.21382 \nL 561.080625 23.077969 \nL 50.980625 23.077969 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: #ffffff\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 74.166989 339.21382 \nL 169.640251 339.21382 \nL 169.640251 244.373065 \nL 74.166989 244.373065 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p230f